           'CyberSanta' Surfs WEB Matching Toys with Kids


NORTH POLE -- December 12, 1996 -- Santa Claus is taking the 
information highway this season to pick toys children most want to 
receive for the holidays.  He's making a list and checking it twice 
on the first Web site that uses advanced technology to custom match 
children's toy preferences with this year's hottest offerings.

     Digital Equipment Corporation and Toys "R" Us have teamed up to 
deliver EachToy, which is aimed at solving the age-old dilemma of 
choosing the right gift for a child.  This unique, interactive Web 
site goes beyond the catalog content of toy retailer Web sites by 
recommending toys, based on a child's likes and dislikes.  Beginning 
today, Santa's helpers can find EachToy on the World Wide Web by 
visiting: http://www.eachtoy.com

     Through a selection process using Digital's Each-to-Each 
technology, children's preferred types of toys are closely matched 
to 400 toys marketed through the Toys "R" Us chain of stores.  
Categories for infants through the teenage years include action 
figures, sporting goods, dolls, educational toys, bikes, and games.

Collaborative Insight

     EachToy is a technology demonstration by Digital's Research and 
Development laboratories in Palo Alto, California and Toys "R" Us, 
the world's largest retailer of children's products.

     "EachToy is fun.  It works like a personalized Internet 
shopping and selection tool," said Robert M. Supnik, Digital's vice 
president of Research and Advanced Development.  "Users at their PCs 
rate how much their children or grandchildren like or dislike a 
series of toys.  The system uses a process called 'collaborative 
filtering' to incorporate their data into an overall preference 
model, and returns a ranked series of toy recommendations based on 
the preferences of a group of kids with similar likes and dislikes," 
he said.

     Toys recommended on the Web site are available at 651 Toys "R" 
Us stores across the country.

Removes Guesswork

     "EachToy greatly simplifies the whole toy selection process for 
parents, grandparents and other toy purchasers," said Anne Cochran, 
manager of Interactive Retailing at Toys "R" Us.  "It allows us to 
explore technologies which can help take much of the guesswork out 
of toy buying for customers who need help in selecting the perfect 
toy for each child on their list."

     Cochran said EachToy will allow Toys "R" Us to evaluate and 
develop powerful new selling tools to deliver personalized 
promotions to its consumers.  "At the same time, the results of the 
companies' efforts will demonstrate how businesses can become more 
successful in electronic commerce," she said.

