           AltaVista Directory '97 Ships for Windows NT --
        Personnel Directory for Business Networks Goes Online


     ...High-Performance Directory Application Supports LDAP and
      Phonetic Searching in Teams and Across the Enterprise...


MAYNARD, Mass., December 10, 1996 -- Expanding its suite of Internet 
software products, Digital Equipment Corporation's AltaVista 
Software Business Unit today announced the shipment of AltaVista 
Directory '97, an intelligent and powerful out-of-the-box personnel 
directory application for Windows NT servers.  AltaVista Directory 
'97 includes phonetic search capabilities and is client-independent. 
Users access it with their favorite Web browser, MAPI, ph and Finger 
email clients, as well as LDAP (Lightweight Directory Access 
Protocol) applications. AltaVista Directory '97 also provides
state-of-the-art management capabilities, making it much faster and 
easier to network, configure and update corporate directories, while 
supporting hundreds of thousands of entries.

     "With AltaVista Directory '97 we are providing one of the most 
intelligent and comprehensive directory management applications 
available today," said Ilene H. Lang, vice president of Digital's 
AltaVista Software Business Unit. "Like a corporate electronic Rolodex, 
AltaVista Directory '97 provides personnel directory capabilities across 
a network to dramatically improve the internal and external communication 
lifelines of a company. This results in tremendous savings of time 
and money."

     The key advantages of AltaVista Directory '97 as compared to 
other directory software applications are its virtually fool-proof, 
out-of-the-box installation and innovative phonetic search 
capabilities. The software is pre-configured to eliminate the 
development typically associated with directory deployment, and is 
uniquely designed to be operational within minutes of installation. 
AltaVista Directory '97 can be integrated seamlessly with other 
applications. Pictures and hyperlinks to Web pages are also 
supported.  Bulkloading directory listings from e-mail systems, HR 
systems, and legacy directories are fast and easy.

     AltaVista Directory '97 users can quickly locate anyone via 
standard Web browsers such as Netscape Navigator and Microsoft 
Explorer, or popular email clients including Eudora and Microsoft 
Exchange. Only one field of information, such as a phone number or 
last name, is required for AltaVista Directory '97 to locate the 
entire listing. AltaVista Directory 97's phonetic search capability 
locates someone even when the user is not sure how to spell the 
name.

     AltaVista Directory '97 is built on open Internet and 
international standards and uses the Hypertext Protocol, HTTP, 
Internet RFC 1777 (LDAP).

Pricing and Availability

     AltaVista Directory '97 is available today. A 30-day trial 
version of the software can be downloaded from the AltaVista 
Software Web site at http://altavista.software.digital.com. It can 
also be purchased through resellers, catalog vendors, ISPs, VARs, 
and Digital Equipment Corporation. Pricing ranges from $495 to 
$3,995.

     AltaVista OnSite Computing solutions provide secure, simple and 
direct access to information and people over the Internet and 
private intranets. AltaVista Search, Directory, Tunnel, Firewall, 
Forum and Mail products give users a competitive edge, enabling 
productive business to take place from anywhere. Further information 
on AltaVista Directory '97 and AltaVista OnSite Computing is 
available at http://altavista.software.digital.com, or by calling 
1-800-336-7890.

