                    Digital Delivers Powerful New
                     Internet Business Solutions


    ...Comprehensive Products, Solutions, and Partnerships Match
                          Customer Needs...


New York, December 11, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
introduced new Internet Business Solutions targeted at three high-
growth Internet market segments - Internet Service Providers 
(ISPs), corporate intranets and Internet commerce. The introductions 
are part of Digital's focus, "bringing business to the Internet," at 
the Internet World trade show here.

     Digital's new solutions enable ISPs to bolster performance and 
reliability of their services and infrastructure, allowing 
organizations to simplify the integration of the Internet into their 
work environments. These products and services also enable 
businesses to implement Internet commerce applications through 
innovative technology and partnerships.

     "Digital is uniquely positioned to bring business to the 
Internet by providing solutions with partners, innovative 
technology, and the best platforms and services in the industry," 
said Rose Ann Giordano, vice president of the Internet Business 
Group.  "Today, we are extending the depth and breadth of our 
Internet Business Solutions, advancing the capability that is 
allowing Digital and our partners to win business worldwide."

The following Internet products and solutions were unveiled today by 
Digital and its partners:

     *	Out-of-the-box "Internet-Energized" Solutions based on 
        Digital's 64-bit AlphaServer system: Included are 
        AlphaServer for Intranet Search, the first hardware/software 
        solution based on the award-winning AltaVista search engine; 
        and three new "Internet Energized" AlphaServer systems 
        available with enhanced system management and clustering 
        capabilities.

     *	Innovative Internet solutions and programs for ISPs: 
        Included are the ISP Startup, a high-availability platform 
        for delivering Internet services; and the ISP Expertise 
        Center, a one-stop source for ISPs providing application 
        integration and technical assistance.

     *	Web partnerships to deliver Internet business solutions: 
        Included are an agreement with Netscape Communications Corp. 
        that makes Netscape SuiteSpot and Commercial Applications 
        available on Digital UNIX AlphaServer systems; an agreement 
        with Microsoft Corp. that makes Merchant Server -- 
        Microsoft's Electronic Commerce solution -- available on 
        Digital Intel and Alpha-based servers; and an agreement 
     	with Oracle Corp. and Digex that provides Internet-based 
        business productivity services using the Oracle InterOffice 
        Suite.

     *	Exciting new customer solutions: Included are a 
        comprehensive project by Digital and its partners to wire 
        major buildings in New York City for high-speed Internet 
        access.

Out-of-the-box Internet Solutions

     Digital is adding significant new features and models to its 
Internet-Energized AlphaServer solutions portfolio.  The Internet-
Energized capability, standard on all AlphaServer systems, provides 
a robust selection of bundled software required to easily create and 
manage an Internet or corporate intranet Web site.  New features 
include:

AlphaServer for Intranet Search Solution

     The new AlphaServer for Intranet Search solution unlocks the 
full potential of corporate intranets. This software/hardware 
ensemble indexes every word in an organization's web pages, enabling 
corporate intranet users to rapidly access the information they 
need.  It integrates the award-winning AltaVista Search Intranet 
Private eXtention software, the record-breaking AlphaServer 4000 
5/400 64-bit RISC system, and the 64-bit Digital UNIX operating 
system.  The solution is available now and is priced at $73,840.

PLUS option

     Customers can now leverage the power and scalability of 
AlphaServer solutions enhanced with the Internet Energized "PLUS" 
option.  This option includes Netscape Enterprise Server software, 
which provides commercial-quality Web site creation and management 
capabilities.  The PLUS option also provides a suite of enhanced 
Internet server management software, including Digital's ServerWorks 
management system and BMC Software's PATROL knowledge Modules for 
Internet Services and PATROL watch for WebBrowser Console.

     The PLUS option also is available with Digital's UNIX 
TruCluster Available Server software, which enables users to operate 
secure, high-availability, dual-node web sites.

     New models include three new AlphaServer systems, initially 
available with the PLUS and high-availability enhanced Internet-
Energized options:  the new AlphaServer 300 4/266 value server, the 
high-capacity AlphaServer 1000A 5/400, and the high-performance 
AlphaServer 4100 5/400 SMP system.  Pricing begins at $6,995; PLUS 
options start at $9,090; dual-node cluster packages start at 
$29,310.

ISP Start-up Solution for Digital UNIX

     Digital today is expanding its offerings in the ISP marketplace 
with its ISP Start-up Solution for Digital UNIX.  The integrated 
software and shared disk design is ideal for a start-up ISP's 
network operation center (NOC) or for existing ISPs needing to 
offload high traffic applications like mail, secure news or web 
hosting. Based on one of the Internet-Energized AlphaServer systems 
with high availability, the ISP Start-up Platform comes rack-mounted 
with factory-installed TruCluster Available Server software on a 
dual AlphaServer 1000A UNIX configuration. The solution is optimized 
to meet the reliability and scalability needs of today's fast 
growing ISPs.  This solution delivers unprecedented per square foot 
compute power in a space-saving rack-mounted package, and optional 
trouble tracking and billing software.

ISP Solution Center

     Digital also announced its ISP Solution Center, a fully 
operational demo, testing and solution integration facility coming 
on-line this month to support ISP projects and customers worldwide.   
With a targeted focus on the ISP market, Digital and its global 
partners expect to accelerate the movement of ISPs to Digital and 
more than double their ISP marketshare. "Our business is growing 
very fast and maintaining high levels of performance for our 
subscribers is paramount," said Tim Jackson, CEO of TIAC, The 
Internet Access Company. "Working with Comport Consulting, one of 
Digital's Internet VARs, we recently installed a pair of AlphaServer 
2100 systems as dedicated mail servers, our most critical 
application. The systems have exceeded our expectations and our 
customers are already experiencing improved performance."

Working With Partners

Netscape

     Digital is now shipping Netscape SuiteSpot, an integrated 
server software suite, and Commercial Applications - Publishing, 
Community, and Merchant - designed to provide partners and customers 
with an integrated modular approach to building Internet and 
intranet applications.  Netscape SuiteSpot components are available 
from Digital on Digital UNIX as well as Windows NT for Alpha and 
Intel.

Microsoft

     Microsoft's Merchant Server, an Internet application for 
Windows NT that enables businesses to create and manage cost-
effective Internet stores, is now available for Digital's Intel 
and Alpha-based servers. In addition to providing the kind of 
high-performance scalable and reliable systems required for Internet 
commerce, Digital offers a variety of services for Merchant Server, 
ranging from assessment and implementation to hosting.  With this 
approach, Digital's customers have maximum flexibility in deploying 
Internet commerce solutions.

Internet Road Map v2.2

     A new version of Digital's Internet Road Map for Windows NT 
offers customers the ability to experience and evaluate Internet 
software on their Windows NT systems before they purchase it.  The 
v2.2 CD contains more than 51 products from more than 25 vendors, 
along with 180 shareware programs and extensive information about 
all aspects of the Internet.  

The CD runs on any Windows NT or Windows 95 system and contains 
software for both Alpha and Intel platforms.  This CD also includes 
a copy of Digital's new FX!32 Alpha translator software.

Oracle

     Digital announced today a technology partnership with Oracle 
and Digex.  This partnership launches Oracle's Interoffice.net which 
is Oracle's Internet-based groupware product running on 
AlphaServers, and is Oracle's premier demo site for this product.  
Interoffice.net allows users to run the integrated office desktop on 
the server.  Oracle's own sales organization is the first 
significant user of this service.

Internet Champions Business Partner Program

     Digital also unveiled the new Internet Champions Business 
Partner Program, a demand-generation initiative designed to make it 
easier and more profitable for value-added resellers (VARS) to sell 
Digital's Internet solutions.  The Program provides marketing 
material and incentives that enable Digital partners to sell more 
servers, software, network products and services.

Internet Innovators

     The Digital Innovators program, introduced at last Fall's 
Internet World in Boston, has reached a milestone in membership with 
the signing of more than 350 partners.  This program was established 
to seek out and support the hot Internet software companies to port 
business solutions to Digital platforms.

Wiring New York for the Internet

     From lower Manhattan to mid-town, New York City is now an 
emerging mecca for multimedia developers and Web-related businesses.
The world's fastest metropolitan Internet access network is 
available right here in New York City. Linked by the fiber-optic 
NYNEX Enterprise backbone, the network is operated by US CYBERSITES, 
Inc., and is built around Digital's GIGAswitch/FDDI system. This 
network offers building owners and tenants in New York City and the 
greater New York metropolitan area unsurpassed, and affordable, 
high-speed switched Internet access.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.

